# Normalise line endings to LF in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checked these files out as CRLF
# while the index held LF. Tests that assert on source text with a regex such as
# `isArchiving,\n\t} = useResumeMutations()` then fail on Windows only, against
# code that is correct — the assertion is matching `\n` and the file has `\r\n`.
# CI runs Linux and never saw it, so the suite was green in one place and red in
# another for the same commit.
#
# Explicit `eol=lf` also stops a Windows checkout from rewriting files on the way
# in, so `git status` stays clean across platforms.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never translate, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Generated artefacts that live in git and must byte-match.
*.min.js binary
*.wasm binary
